    "Prefix and state helpers remain outlined; each prefix call reloads the bound plan/view pointers and runtime chunk/route fields. State selects a prepared point plan by row modulo 16; generic slot/transfer/map interpretation remains. This is residual composition work, not a dataformat timing verdict.",
    "Wide reverse decodes the selected group once and materializes 32 B u16 widths for bounded scalar owner walk. Tuple64 adds outlined dead() for the selected owner. No repeated point geometry read occurs in this walk.",
    "Update driver calls tuple64 dead() then metadata-update; controls read dead inline and call only metadata-update. All update drivers use the same preallocated 512 B journal. Group update helper is call-free, but scans 54 B write-mask coordinates and executes generic prepared point-writer paths.",
    "For Width4095, tuple64 writes the selected low-used byte, shared high-used nibble byte and dead byte: 3 effect runs / 3 issued bytes. Native planes use 2 runs / 3 issued bytes. Series covers 6 issued bytes with 2\u20133 runs because the last row body byte can coalesce with its shared tail. Sibling bits survive; these are issued write/effect costs, not changed-bit counts."
